  "notes": "A godan verb (く row) meaning to act against or turn away from. The core image is of turning one's back ({背|せ}) on something. Used with the particle に to indicate what is being defied or betrayed.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {命令|めいれい}に{背|そむ}く — to disobey an order\n- {期待|きたい}に{背|そむ}く — to go against expectations\n- {信頼|しんらい}に{背|そむ}く — to betray trust\n- ルールに{背|そむ}く — to break the rules\n- {道|みち}に{背|そむ}く — to go against what is right\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {逆|さか}らう — to resist, oppose; implies active resistance or defiance, while {背|そむ}く focuses on going contrary to expectations or loyalty\n- {裏切|うらぎ}る — to betray; stronger and more dramatic, often used for personal betrayals",
